      "realist_desc": "18 hrs / period, standard events. Default.",
      "transportation_desc": "Maine's largest direct emissions source (about 50% of state CO₂ output). Long rural commutes, limited transit, near-zero passenger rail. EV adoption is climbing but still under 5% of registrations. The bigger lever may be reducing vehicle-miles-traveled through housing density and remote work.",
      "workingLands_desc": "Maine is 89% forested, the most forested state by percentage. Working forests sequester roughly 6 million tons CO₂ annually. Agricultural soils, salt marshes, and seagrass beds are smaller but additive carbon sinks. This is one of Maine's climate advantages most states lack."
