      "enceladus_saturn_moon": "Enceladus (Saturn moon)",
      "engineering_fixes_a_full_cut_off_fixtu": "Engineering fixes: (a) FULL CUT-OFF fixtures (light directed ONLY downward, no light escaping above horizontal). The IDA-approved \"Dark Sky Friendly\" certification specifies this. (b) WARMER LED color temperature (≤ 3000 K, ideally 2200 K amber). Cooler/whiter light (4000-6000 K) scatters more in the atmosphere + harms wildlife circadian rhythms. (c) LOWER lumen output (most outdoor lighting is over-lit by 2-5×). (d) MOTION-ACTIVATED + scheduled DIMMING (light only when needed). (e) Avoid uplighting of buildings + landscape features. Phoenix, Tucson, Flagstaff (since 1958 — the FIRST dark-sky city), and parts of Hawaii (around Mauna Kea) have effective lighting ordinances. The International Dark-Sky Association (IDA, founded 1988) certifies \"International Dark-Sky Places\" — about 200 communities + parks worldwide as of 2024.",
      "epsilon_eridani": "Epsilon Eridani",
