      "students_who_lose_interest_try_the_qui": "Students who lose interest: try the Quiz tab. Self-paced + immediate feedback works for many disengaged students.\n\nStudents overwhelmed by content: simplify. Use the Glossary + Vocabulary tabs as scaffolding. Don't need to cover everything in 2 weeks.\n\nStudents skeptical of \"interesting facts\": connect to primary research. Show the citations. Trace claims back to peer-reviewed papers. This builds science literacy.\n\nStudents resistant to ethics topics: be patient. Use the Debate Prompts to depersonalize. Take a position THEY don't hold, then defend it. This builds empathy + understanding.\n\nStudents from different backgrounds: emphasize SHARED human curiosity. Cephalopods are interesting to people from every culture + every economic background. The Cultural Refs tab can help.\n\nStudents asking \"but what's on the TEST?\" — direct them to the Exam Prep tab. Let them see what's being assessed + why.",
      "studies_on_octopus_learning_include_bo": "Studies on octopus learning include both POSITIVE and NEGATIVE reinforcement. Octopuses learn faster with positive reinforcement (food rewards).",
