      "travel_literature": "Travel Literature",
      "triple_impression_printing_was_3_the_l": "Triple-impression printing was 3× the labor + 3× the registration challenges of normal text printing. Petrucci's books were beautiful + expensive — accessible only to wealthy patrons + institutional libraries. Within decades simpler methods (single-impression with notes integrated into staff-line sorts) emerged + dominated commercial music printing. Petrucci's legacy: he proved music could be printed; the specific method gave way to cheaper alternatives.",
